The Java audio device module records from an AudioRecord it makes itself, of the audio source
given to its builder. A share's sound on Android is what other apps play, captured through
AudioPlaybackCaptureConfiguration, which only an AudioRecord.Builder can be configured for, so
the builder takes an AudioRecordFactory that makes the AudioRecord instead, with the format and
buffer size the module would have given its own (client/packages/mobile/android/app/src/main/java/
com/aspen_chat/client/call/CallScreen.kt makes one for each share). Applied to the checkout by
scripts/webrtc_build.py; docs/development/webrtc-build.md says why.

